CORE-001 Protocol — NOTICE
========================

Attribution
-----------
This specification and its reference implementation build on, and align
with, published work of others. Where alignment is claimed, the alignment
is stated in the specification and is independently re-checkable by the
implementer. No affiliation with, endorsement by, or certification from
the following organizations is claimed.

Standards and mechanisms referenced
-----------------------------------
- RFC 6962 / RFC 9162 — Certificate Transparency, Merkle tree
  (Merkle Tree Head, inclusion and consistency proofs)
- RFC 8785 — JSON Canonicalization Scheme (JCS)
- RFC 6920 — Naming Things with Hashes
- RFC 8446 — TLS 1.3 downgrade sentinel (used as a design pattern)
- RFC 6916 — Cross-log anchoring (used as a design pattern)
- DSSE v1.0.2 — Dead Simple Signing Envelope (pre-authentication encoding)
- C2SP tlog-tiles, signed-note, tlog-cosignature
- SLSA — DigestSet
- NIST SP 800-131A — algorithm transition states
- Sigstore Rekor — entry UUID and idempotency conventions
- protobuf — field-number tombstone convention
- FastCDC — content-defined chunking (evaluated)

